{"type":"telemetry","at":"2026-02-20T03:51:20.940634+00:00","payload":{"level":"info","message":"[notifications] full payload","args":["[notifications] full payload",{"notification":{"type":"issue_created","issue_id":"tskl-l82.8","issue_data":{"id":"tskl-l82.8","title":"New browser tabs receive last-known navigation state via SSE replay on connect","description":"Given the local console server is running\nAnd a CLI command previously focused an issue (kbs console focus tskl-abc)\n\nWhen a new browser tab opens the console at the base URL (no deep link)\n\nThen the server sends the last-known UI state as an SSE event on the realtime channel\nAnd the browser navigates to the corresponding URL (e.g., /issues/tskl-abc?focused=tskl-abc)\n\nThis is optional behavior -- if no prior state exists, the browser just shows the default board.\nThis only applies to the local console server. A cloud version would not need this -- users would\nshare URLs directly or the app would maintain per-user state separately.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- On SSE connection, the server replays the last ui_control/focus event to new subscribers\n- The frontend handles this the same way it handles any other SSE event (navigate to URL)\n- No special /api/ui-state endpoint needed","type":"story","status":"open","priority":2,"assignee":null,"creator":"ryan.porter","parent":"tskl-l82","labels":[],"dependencies":[{"target":"tskl-l82","type":"parent-child"}],"comments":[],"created_at":"2026-02-20T03:51:20.938275Z","updated_at":"2026-02-20T03:51:20.938275Z","closed_at":null,"custom":{}}},"hasIssueData":true}],"timestamp":"2026-02-20T03:51:20.939Z","url":"http://localhost:4242/epics/","session_id":"akshkv7w"}}
