{"type":"telemetry","at":"2026-02-20T04:06:34.556203+00:00","payload":{"level":"info","message":"[notifications] full payload","args":["[notifications] full payload",{"notification":{"type":"issue_updated","issue_id":"tskl-l82.7","fields_changed":["status"],"issue_data":{"id":"tskl-l82.7","title":"Search query and focused issue are encoded in the URL so any state can be reached via deep link","description":"Given a user is viewing the console board with a search query active\n\nWhen I copy the URL from the browser address bar\nAnd open it in a new tab\n\nThen the new tab renders the same search results\n\nGiven an issue is focused (showing issue and descendants)\n\nWhen I copy the URL from the browser address bar\nAnd open it in a new tab\n\nThen the new tab shows the same focused issue and its descendants\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- Search query is encoded as a query parameter: ?search=<query>\n- Focused issue is encoded in the URL path (already partially works via /issues/:parentId/all pattern)\n- View mode is in the URL path (already works)\n- On page load, the frontend reads ALL state from the URL and renders accordingly\n- Refreshing the page preserves the complete UI state\n- This means SSE ui_control events just trigger URL changes, and the frontend renders from the URL","type":"story","status":"done","priority":2,"assignee":null,"creator":"ryan.porter","parent":"tskl-l82","labels":[],"dependencies":[],"comments":[],"created_at":"2026-02-20T03:15:49.745499Z","updated_at":"2026-02-20T04:06:34.541052Z","closed_at":null,"custom":{"beads_owner":"ryan.porter"}}},"hasIssueData":true}],"timestamp":"2026-02-20T04:06:34.554Z","url":"http://localhost:4242/issues/","session_id":"akshkv7w"}}
