{"type":"telemetry","at":"2026-02-20T04:17:27.470146+00:00","payload":{"level":"info","message":"[notifications] full payload","args":["[notifications] full payload",{"notification":{"type":"issue_updated","issue_id":"tskl-l82.1","fields_changed":["status"],"issue_data":{"id":"tskl-l82.1","title":"Console server tracks canonical UI state across all connected clients","description":"Given the console server is running\nAnd one or more browser clients are connected via SSE\n\nWhen a CLI command changes the focused issue, view mode, or search query\nThen the server constructs a URL route encoding the full desired UI state\nAnd pushes that route to all connected clients via SSE\nAnd each client navigates to the URL and renders the corresponding state\n\nThe server also caches the last-pushed route in a ConsoleUiState struct so CLI query commands can read it.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- Server holds a ConsoleUiState struct containing: focused_issue_id, view_mode, search_query\n- On receiving a state-changing notification (IssueFocused, ClearFocus, SetViewMode, SetSearch), the server constructs a URL route and pushes it via SSE\n- The frontend navigates to the pushed URL -- this is the only mechanism for server-to-client state changes\n- Two browser tabs opened simultaneously both navigate to the same URL after kbs console focus <id>\n- No backwards-compatibility with the old fire-and-forget notification model","type":"story","status":"done","priority":2,"assignee":null,"creator":"ryan.porter","parent":"tskl-l82","labels":[],"dependencies":[],"comments":[],"created_at":"2026-02-20T03:15:10.413271Z","updated_at":"2026-02-20T04:17:27.453607Z","closed_at":null,"custom":{"beads_owner":"ryan.porter"}}},"hasIssueData":true}],"timestamp":"2026-02-20T04:17:27.469Z","url":"http://localhost:4242/issues/","session_id":"2tibkwq8"}}
{"type":"telemetry","at":"2026-02-20T04:17:27.585126+00:00","payload":{"level":"info","message":"[notifications] received","args":["[notifications] received",{"type":"issue_updated","receivedAt":"2026-02-20T04:17:27.584Z","issueId":"tskl-l82.2"}],"timestamp":"2026-02-20T04:17:27.584Z","url":"http://localhost:4242/issues/","session_id":"2tibkwq8"}}
{"type":"telemetry","at":"2026-02-20T04:17:27.587243+00:00","payload":{"level":"info","message":"[notifications] full payload","args":["[notifications] full payload",{"notification":{"type":"issue_updated","issue_id":"tskl-l82.2","fields_changed":["status"],"issue_data":{"id":"tskl-l82.2","title":"Console server saves and restores UI state from .kanbus/.cache/console_state.json","description":"Given a console server that has been running with some UI state\n(e.g., an issue is focused, a view mode is set)\n\nWhen the server is stopped and restarted\n\nThen the server reads the last-pushed route from .kanbus/.cache/console_state.json at startup\nAnd replays that route to clients that connect via SSE\nAnd kbs console get focus returns the same focused issue as before the restart\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- ConsoleUiState (the cache of the last-pushed route) is persisted to .kanbus/.cache/console_state.json after every mutation\n- State is loaded from that file at server startup (file missing = default empty state, no error)\n- File format is JSON, human-readable\n- On restart, the restored state is replayed to new SSE subscribers as a route push","type":"story","status":"done","priority":2,"assignee":null,"creator":"ryan.porter","parent":"tskl-l82","labels":[],"dependencies":[],"comments":[],"created_at":"2026-02-20T03:15:16.338693Z","updated_at":"2026-02-20T04:17:27.508197Z","closed_at":null,"custom":{"beads_owner":"ryan.porter"}}},"hasIssueData":true}],"timestamp":"2026-02-20T04:17:27.584Z","url":"http://localhost:4242/issues/","session_id":"2tibkwq8"}}
