{"type":"telemetry","at":"2026-02-20T04:54:06.145480+00:00","payload":{"level":"info","message":"[notifications] full payload","args":["[notifications] full payload",{"notification":{"type":"issue_updated","issue_id":"tskl-l82.9","fields_changed":["status"],"issue_data":{"id":"tskl-l82.9","title":"Deep link to specific comment within an issue via URL and CLI","description":"Given an agent has added a comment to an issue\n\nWhen the agent runs kbs console focus tskl-abc --comment 8ea9cd\n\nThen the CLI sends a notification through the server\nAnd the server pushes a URL route to all connected clients: /issues/tskl-abc?focused=tskl-abc&comment=8ea9cd\nAnd the browser navigates to that URL\nAnd the detail panel opens to the issue\nAnd the panel scrolls to the specified comment\nAnd the comment is visually highlighted\n\nGiven a user opens a URL with a comment parameter directly in their browser\n\nWhen the URL contains ?comment=8ea9cd\n\nThen the same scroll-to and highlight behavior occurs\n\nThis extends the URL-as-state model to sub-issue elements. The comment parameter is the first\nsuch element but the pattern should support future element types (e.g., a specific field change).\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- kbs console focus accepts an optional --comment <id> flag\n- Comment ID is encoded as ?comment=<id> query parameter in the URL\n- Frontend parses ?comment= on load and on SSE-pushed route changes\n- Detail panel scrolls to the comment and highlights it (existing highlight animation can be reused)\n- Works on initial page load (pasting URL) and on SSE push (agent workflow)","type":"story","status":"in_progress","priority":2,"assignee":null,"creator":"ryan.porter","parent":"tskl-l82","labels":[],"dependencies":[],"comments":[{"id":"6f9b18b0-fec2-585a-b2ac-26b2a823f70a","author":"ryan.porter","text":"Implemented comment deep linking. Added --comment <id> flag to kbs console focus. comment_id is passed through IssueFocused event, tracked in ConsoleUiState, persisted, and replayed on SSE connect. Frontend reads ?comment= from URL, passes focusedCommentId to TaskDetailPanel which scrolls to and highlights the target comment with an outline animation. Full round-trip: kbs console focus tskl-abc --comment 8ea9cd -> server -> SSE -> browser scrolls to comment.","created_at":"2026-02-20T04:37:19.578695Z"}],"created_at":"2026-02-20T03:55:33.124149Z","updated_at":"2026-02-20T04:54:06.131443Z","closed_at":null,"custom":{"beads_owner":"ryan.porter"}}},"hasIssueData":true}],"timestamp":"2026-02-20T04:54:06.144Z","url":"http://localhost:4242/epics/","session_id":"3dphpfk0"}}
